    "bottomLine": "The low-cost everyday filter for homes without allergies: good dust capture with minimal airflow restriction.",
    "description": "MERV 8 is the baseline most HVAC makers are designed around, and the Filterbuy MERV 8 is a well-built, low-cost way to meet it. Filterbuy lists it as comparable to Filtrete's MPR 700 and Honeywell's FPR 5, and says its synthetic MERV 8 media captures 90 percent of dust without restricting airflow, which is the main reason to choose MERV 8: it protects the furnace and catches household dust, pollen, lint and mold spores with the least strain on the blower. The media is electrostatically charged with 14 pleats per foot, which Filterbuy says traps more microscopic particles and lasts three times longer than fiberglass filters. Construction is a step above flimsy cardboard: a beverage board frame with dual wire backing is designed to resist warping and extreme temperatures, which matters in hot attics and cold garages. It is made in the USA, per the listing, and the recommended change interval is every 90 days. The actual size is 15.50 x 24.50 x 0.75 inches, so as always, compare against the size printed on your current filter. The trade-off is fine-particle capture. If anyone in the home has allergies or asthma, or you have pets, step up to the Filtrete MERV 11 or a MERV 13. Buy the Aerostar MERV 13 instead for allergies at a similar per-filter cost."
