    "description": "Filtrete's MPR 1900 is its highest-filtration everyday filter, rated MERV 13, and it is our pick for homes where allergies are the main reason for buying. The listing gives a 62 percent capture rate for microparticles between 0.3 and 1 micron, the size range of fine dust, smoke and many allergens, and says the filter is certified asthma and allergy friendly. Its strongest selling point is airflow. Filtrete says the MPR 1900 delivers better airflow than any other brand's residential 1-inch retail MERV 13 filter, based on California Energy Commission data, which matters because airflow restriction is the main drawback of high-MERV filters. Filtrete also notes it was selected as a top pick by The New York Times Wirecutter. Like the MPR 1000, it is a pleated 3-month filter that should be changed at least every 90 days, with Smart App reminders available, and the listing gives the actual size as 15.62 x 24.62 x 0.78 inches. Two cautions: it is the most expensive disposable filter here, and the listing title says four filters while the feature text describes a single filter, so check the pack count before ordering. Ignore the packaging's bacteria and virus claims as a reason to buy. Buy the Aerostar MERV 13 instead for a lower cost per filter."
  },
  {
    "id": "nordic-pure-merv-12-plus-carbon",
    "name": "Nordic Pure MERV 12 Plus Carbon Air Filter (16x25x1, 6-Pack)",
    "category": "MERV 12 with Activated Carbon, Pleated, Made in USA",
