          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "MERV 11 is the best balance for most homes: much better dust and dander capture than MERV 8 without much airflow penalty. MERV 13 suits allergy sufferers and smoke where the system can handle it. MERV 8 is fine for homes without allergies or pets. Check your HVAC manual before going above MERV 11."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a higher MERV filter bad for my furnace?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not usually, if your system is designed for it and you change the filter on time. Higher MERV filters restrict airflow more, which can strain older or undersized systems. A clogged filter of any rating is worse than a clean high-MERV one. Ask a technician if your system struggles."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How often should I change my furnace filter?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most 1-inch pleated filters are rated for up to about 90 days. Change every 30 to 60 days with pets, allergies, smokers or heavy use. Check monthly by holding the filter up to the light, and change it if light no longer passes through."
          }
