        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the best furnace filter for allergies?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A MERV 13 filter, like the Filtrete MPR 1900 or Aerostar MERV 13, captures the finest allergens a 1-inch filter can. The Filtrete MPR 1900 lists a 62 percent capture rate for 0.3 to 1 micron particles. Pair it with a HEPA air purifier in the bedroom for the best results."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are washable furnace filters worth it?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "They can be if you dislike buying filters and will wash them on schedule. The K&N MERV 11 is rated equal to good disposable filters, and K&N lists about $30 a year in savings. The catch is drying time: the filter must be fully dry before refitting, so many owners keep a spare."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which way does the arrow go on a furnace filter?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The airflow arrow points toward the furnace, in the direction air travels, away from the return duct. Installing it backwards reduces filtration and can damage the filter. Check before closing the slot."
